  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 was weakened from a sales-stop to a review trigger, so the Hearth 10 (6.2% failure) can keep selling, and per-model results go to regulators and purchasers but not the public. S3's 6-year retrofit deadline (within the acceptable range, not the safe 3-year one) favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100k with no transition, which directly exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9 per 100k); S1 is strict (24-hour reporting) for both companies."
